{"format_version":"vbulletin-3+-thread","url":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/trinity/trinity-continuum-\u00e6on/148684-what-i-want-to-see-in-a-new-aeon-trinity-reboot","id":148684,"title":"What I want to see in a new Aeon Trinity reboot.","path":["Home","Onyx Path","Onyx Path Worlds","The Trinity Continuum","Trinity Continuum: \u00c6on"],"posts":[{"date":"2014-05-25T07:39:33-07:00","id":148684,"title":"What I want to see in a new Aeon Trinity reboot.","content":"Hi there. Just stumbled over the old rpg.net thread <a href=\"http://forum.rpg.net/showthread.php?664550-Trinity-reboot-What-do-you-want-to-see\" target=\"_blank\">http://forum.rpg.net/showthread.php?...ou-want-to-see</a> and thought I' add my personal wishes. So why not do it here. <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/smile.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Smile\" smilieid=\"1\" class=\"inlineimg\" /><br /> <br /> <span style=\"font-family:Helvetica\"><span style=\"font-size:12px\">REGARDING APTITUDES:</span></span><br /> <span style=\"font-family:Helvetica\"><span style=\"font-size:12px\">Being dunked in a Prometheus Chamber limits a psion to one aptitude. I like this for gaming reasons: There will be no super-duper-100-aptitudes-kick-ass psions, which forces the players to work together to solve a problem. Sort of a scissor-paper-rock situation.</span></span><br /> <br /> <span style=\"font-family:Helvetica\"><span style=\"font-size:12px\">Having said that, I would like some mechanics for psions which are NOT limited to one aptitude (I don\u2019t mean auxiliary modes here).</span></span><br /> <br /> <span style=\"font-family:Helvetica\"><span style=\"font-size:12px\">Also, full rules for Quantakinetics please.</span></span><br /> <br /> <span style=\"font-family:Helvetica\"><span style=\"font-size:12px\">Finally, a understandable and easy-to-use freeform rules would be great. The one in the Players Guide was a mess. I just couldn\u2019t get all the different tables in my head. A system which needs constant table consulting is unuseable.</span></span><br /> <br /> <span style=\"font-family:Helvetica\"><span style=\"font-size:12px\">REGARDING TELEPORTATION:</span></span><br /> <span style=\"font-family:Helvetica\"><span style=\"font-size:12px\">I always disliked the time-delay aspect of theTranslocation mode, especially since Transmassion was instantenous. I\u2019d house rule it at least to be quicker with each dot in Translocation.</span></span><br /> <br /> <span style=\"font-family:Helvetica\"><span style=\"font-size:12px\">Also, the familiarity rule is kind of draconic. I understand that these restrictions try to prevent Teleportation from being overpowered, but it still doesn\u2019t\u2026 feel right (especially after reading the Jumper series from Steven Gould).</span></span><br /> <br /> <span style=\"font-family:Helvetica\"><span style=\"font-size:12px\">REGARDING BIOKINESIS:</span></span><br /> <span style=\"font-family:Helvetica\"><span style=\"font-size:12px\">I never understood why Biokinetics weren\u2019t able to heal themselves. Yeah yeah, that\u2019s the domain of the Vitakinetics, but still. They can grow additional limbs and organs, so why not close their wounds. Does. Not. Make. Sense. (I know that the free mode rules allowed this, but Terra Verde didn\u2019t include them anymore.)</span></span><br /> <br /> <span style=\"font-family:Helvetica\"><span style=\"font-size:12px\">REGARDING TIMETABLES/SETTINGS:</span></span><br /> <span style=\"font-family:Helvetica\"><span style=\"font-size:12px\">I like the idea about the different time setting between Adventure!, Aberrant and Trinity. But why are the rules (about Daredevils, Psions, Novas) bound to their setting? How about the rules to support e.g.Psions in the pulp era, and even completely new settings, like Steven Otte\u2019s Milleniums Edge 2997?</span></span><br /> <br /> <span style=\"font-family:Helvetica\"><span style=\"font-size:12px\">CROSSOVERS:</span></span><br /> <span style=\"font-family:Helvetica\"><span style=\"font-size:12px\">Support for all splats (Daredevils, Psions, Novas) to be played in crossover mode. I suppose that a Nova will always outpower your average Psion, but what the heck.</span></span><br /> <br /> <span style=\"font-family:Helvetica\"><span style=\"font-size:12px\">ALIENS:</span></span><br /> <span style=\"font-family:Helvetica\"><span style=\"font-size:12px\">I\u2019d like rules for aliens (Chromatics, Qin) to be playable as PCs, especially when playing in the far, far future.</span></span><br /> <br /> <span style=\"font-family:Helvetica\"><span style=\"font-size:12px\">SUPPLEMENTS:</span></span><br /> <span style=\"font-family:Helvetica\"><span style=\"font-size:12px\">Will there be any more supplements, like the Trinity Order/Region books? I always missed that Africa didn\u2019t get their share of love.<br /> <br /> AND... ACTION!:<br /> Maybe this doesn't belong here. But I didn't like the sparse Psi points, resulting in the PCs to use their powers maybe three times a day or so. I'd give the players the Merit Mode Natural (7 points) for free for one mode. Results in a bit more ... cinematic action. Let's see how the reboot handles this.</span></span>","signature":"","edited":{"userid":3122,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3122-shuragil","user":"shuragil","date":". 05-25-2014, 10:59 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3122-shuragil","name":"shuragil","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"41"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-05-25T08:04:49-07:00","id":148700,"title":"","content":"I believe that many of these things are going to be included in Trinity Continuum, so your wish will probably be granted!","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2464-lustral_star","name":"lustral_star","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2464_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"302"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-05-25T09:33:22-07:00","id":148740,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>shuragil</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/trinity/trinity-continuum-\u00e6on/148684-what-i-want-to-see-in-a-new-aeon-trinity-reboot#post148684\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Being dunked in a Prometheus Chamber limits a psion to one aptitude.</div> </div> </div> </div>That's been part of the setting since 1997.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> I always disliked the time-delay aspect of the Translocation mode, especially since Transmassion was instantenous. I\u2019d house rule it at least to be quicker with each dot in Translocation. </div> </div> </div>There's no guarantee that Teleportation will even have the same modes.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> Will there be any more supplements, like the Trinity Order/Region books? I always missed that Africa didn\u2019t get their share of love. </div> </div> </div>The new edition will have plenty of supplements. The old edition will not.<br /> <br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b><span style=\"color:#800000\">Ian A. A. Watson</span></b><span style=\"color:#bdc3c7\">(he/she)</span><br /> <b>Onyx Path Community Manager<br /> Trinity Continuum Content Lead</b>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4-ianwatson","name":"IanWatson","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar4_2.png","title":"Community Manager","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1512"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-05-25T09:53:59-07:00","id":148747,"title":"","content":"Much appreciated, Ian.<br /> <br /> In addition, with regards to the request for rules for psions who are not limited to one aptitude: I recall reading information about that somewhere. I think it was in the Aberrant Player's Guide? Around page 60, I believe.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2464-lustral_star","name":"lustral_star","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2464_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"302"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-05-27T07:02:27-07:00","id":150292,"title":"","content":"As someone with no connection whatsoever to the game and only paid it attention after the mention it wil use similar mechanics to Scion I went and had a skim of the old Aeon book.<br /> <br /> A thing I noticed was that I'd basically never want to play as most of the archetypes. Not to say I wouldn't want someone with their powers...just not someone who <i>only</i> had those powers. Mostly it comes down to having some kind of cool visual flashy power to go along with something more cerebral. A Clarisentient for example is really cool...until I realised all I'd be doing in my minds eye is grimacing a lot.<br /> <br /> So I'd like to see something that makes it easy to get something flashier either in each of the archetypes or have the entry level powers of each of the different archetypes be flashier or more powerful. See how Blood and Smoke makes rank 1 in a Discipline a boiled down essentials version of each theme. So someone who is a full on Clarisentient could also grab something on the side for Biokinesis or the like that bonus power doesn't feel like something really boring like moderately altering the temperature.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/291-scutarii","name":"Scutarii","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar291_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"702"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-06-09T13:01:21-07:00","id":163928,"title":"","content":"For starters, a good indicator of powerscales would be nice, I've recently had to fudge alot in 1st ed Trinity. Something I am not really used to coming from D&amp;D 3rd, 3.5 and 4th edition (which frankly did wonders for balance in that game). Some combative powers for each order would be nice. Not saying every order should have powers that do MASSIVE DAMAGE just something to aid combat a bit is what I'd like.<br /> <br /> And...please...PLEASE fix the weapon damage scale for vehicles. I spent over 3 hours just a few days ago overhauling it for my game because I couldn't stand the fact that a fighter has gun that does the same damage as those mounted on a frigate.<br /> <br /> Otherwise I'm more curious to see what ya fella's come up with, I can only critique something once I know what it is. And I ain't no Clear.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><i>Man's unfailing capacity to believe what he prefers to be true rather than what the evidence shows to be likely and possible has always astounded me. We long for a caring Universe which will save us from our childish mistakes, and in the face of mountains of evidence to the contrary we will pin all our hopes on the slimmest of doubts. God has not been proven not to exist, therefore he must exist.</i> <b>--Academician Prokhor Zakharov</b>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3246-galaxy-master-zhad","name":"Galaxy Master Zhad","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3246_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"37"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-06-11T09:36:11-07:00","id":166016,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>lustral_star</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/trinity/trinity-continuum-\u00e6on/148684-what-i-want-to-see-in-a-new-aeon-trinity-reboot?p=148747#post148747\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Much appreciated, Ian.<br /> <br /> In addition, with regards to the request for rules for psions who are not limited to one aptitude: I recall reading information about that somewhere. I think it was in the Aberrant Player's Guide? Around page 60, I believe.</div> </div> </div> </div>Those are psiads. They aren't dunked. They occur naturally, but aren't as focused, so they don't reach the extremes of power that the Prometheus Chambers allow.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/23-saur-ops-specialist","name":"Saur Ops Specialist","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar23_3.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"9371"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-06-11T17:10:08-07:00","id":166363,"title":"","content":"While there's something of an origin difference between psiads and psions (and depending on what you're doing with plot, the two of them have slightly different roles in the order of things), they might be appropriate for shuragil's uses -- whatever they might be. Just as long as he uses the rules for psionic Aptitudes and not individual Powers.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2464-lustral_star","name":"lustral_star","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2464_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"302"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-06-25T22:44:48-07:00","id":180453,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>shuragil</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/trinity/trinity-continuum-\u00e6on/148684-what-i-want-to-see-in-a-new-aeon-trinity-reboot#post148684\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Hi there. Just stumbled over the old rpg.net thread <a href=\"http://forum.rpg.net/showthread.php?664550-Trinity-reboot-What-do-you-want-to-see\" target=\"_blank\">http://forum.rpg.net/showthread.php?...ou-want-to-see</a> and thought I' add my personal wishes. So why not do it here. <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/smile.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Smile\" smilieid=\"1\" class=\"inlineimg\" /><br /> <br /> <span style=\"font-family:Helvetica\"><span style=\"font-size:12px\">REGARDING APTITUDES:</span></span><br /> <span style=\"font-family:Helvetica\"><span style=\"font-size:12px\">Being dunked in a Prometheus Chamber limits a psion to one aptitude. I like this for gaming reasons: There will be no super-duper-100-aptitudes-kick-ass psions, which forces the players to work together to solve a problem. Sort of a scissor-paper-rock situation.</span></span><br /> <br /> <span style=\"font-family:Helvetica\"><span style=\"font-size:12px\">Having said that, I would like some mechanics for psions which are NOT limited to one aptitude (I don\u2019t mean auxiliary modes here).</span></span><br /> <br /> <span style=\"font-family:Helvetica\"><span style=\"font-size:12px\">Also, full rules for Quantakinetics please.</span></span><br /> <br /> <span style=\"font-family:Helvetica\"><span style=\"font-size:12px\">Finally, a understandable and easy-to-use freeform rules would be great. The one in the Players Guide was a mess. I just couldn\u2019t get all the different tables in my head. A system which needs constant table consulting is unuseable.</span></span></div> </div> </div> </div>You should be very pleased with Aeon then. There will eventually be rules for Psiads, but the core Aeon book will be all about Psions who were dunked in Prometheus Tanks and who are awesome at one Aptitude. <br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <span style=\"font-family:Helvetica\"><span style=\"font-size:12px\">REGARDING BIOKINESIS:</span></span><br /> <span style=\"font-family:Helvetica\"><span style=\"font-size:12px\">I never understood why Biokinetics weren\u2019t able to heal themselves. Yeah yeah, that\u2019s the domain of the Vitakinetics, but still. They can grow additional limbs and organs, so why not close their wounds. Does. Not. Make. Sense. (I know that the free mode rules allowed this, but Terra Verde didn\u2019t include them anymore.)</span></span> </div> </div> </div>I entirely agree.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <span style=\"font-family:Helvetica\"><span style=\"font-size:12px\">CROSSOVERS:</span></span><br /> <span style=\"font-family:Helvetica\"><span style=\"font-size:12px\">Support for all splats (Daredevils, Psions, Novas) to be played in crossover mode. I suppose that a Nova will always outpower your average Psion, but what the heck.</span></span> </div> </div> </div>Don't expect support for playing Novas in Aeon anytime soon, since the Nova rules won't come out until Aberrant is released. However, the Aeon book will be released at the same time as the TU core book, which will have rules for Talents (aka Daredevils). I'd definitely be foolish if I didn't include a discussion of including Talents in Aeon. However, the focus of the Aeon book will be on Psions.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <span style=\"font-family:Helvetica\"><span style=\"font-size:12px\">ALIENS:</span></span><br /> <span style=\"font-family:Helvetica\"><span style=\"font-size:12px\">I\u2019d like rules for aliens (Chromatics, Qin) to be playable as PCs, especially when playing in the far, far future.</span></span> </div> </div> </div>Again, don't expect this soon, but eventually having rules for playing Chromatics, Qin, and possibly some Phyle of Coalition are definitely in my plans.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> Maybe this doesn't belong here. But I didn't like the sparse Psi points, resulting in the PCs to use their powers maybe three times a day or so. I'd give the players the Merit Mode Natural (7 points) for free for one mode. Results in a bit more ... cinematic action. Let's see how the reboot handles this.[/SIZE][/FONT] </div> </div> </div>The psi power rules are being completely reworked. The goal is to make them both simple and relatively freeform (I consider the freeform rules in the PG to be hellishly complex and are the sort of thing I would never personally use). The TU is a setting of cinematic action, and so the goal is for psi powers to be very much part of that.<br /> <br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/96-john-snead","name":"John Snead","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar96_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"34"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-07-04T16:59:49-07:00","id":188315,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>shuragil</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/trinity/trinity-continuum-\u00e6on/148684-what-i-want-to-see-in-a-new-aeon-trinity-reboot#post148684\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><span style=\"font-family:Helvetica\"><span style=\"font-size:12px\">REGARDING BIOKINESIS:</span></span><br /> <span style=\"font-family:Helvetica\"><span style=\"font-size:12px\">I never understood why Biokinetics weren\u2019t able to heal themselves. Yeah yeah, that\u2019s the domain of the Vitakinetics, but still. They can grow additional limbs and organs, so why not close their wounds. Does. Not. Make. Sense. (I know that the free mode rules allowed this, but Terra Verde didn\u2019t include them anymore.)</span></span></div> </div> </div> </div>I always assumed that BioKinetics could close wounds with the corret powers (If you can gown a new leg, or make a leg into a stump, or grow wings, you could grow a unbroken leg from a broken one) but they would be moving the damage around rather than healing it (they would still have the damage boxes and the negatives).<br /> <br /> If the limits seemed contrived and artifical that's because they are. Just like telepaths cannot cure mental trama.<br /> <br /> That being said I imagine it is was a challenge for the writers to create the limits and if I designed a game I would probably not have placed them in the same places and I often feel like the Trinity books did not have the same polish as some of the other lines. Not that I am going to critisize from the cheap seats but my observation for what it is worth.<br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3424-patrick-chapman","name":"Patrick Chapman","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-07-09T23:47:53-07:00","id":193218,"title":"","content":"What I'd like to see... in no particular order... (warning, some of these are petty; I make no apology for my nitpicking! This is how I show my love!)<br /> <br /> 1. Some clarity over the distinction between psionically-active &quot;biotech&quot; and plain ol' biotechnology. There were hints of this in the original edition; biotech &quot;Enamel&quot; knives had no Formatted Tolerance rating because they were, ostensibly, just really hard organic enamel in the shape of a knife. I loved the idea that true psitech could become parasitic, so characters had to manage their Tolerance ratings.<br /> <br /> 2. Better story-mechanics transparency. The original Trinity (Aeon) book fell flat on a few measures. The ones that stood out to me were: a) biokinetics boasted they had need for vitakinetics in story (maybe they were lying!), but had no healing powers in their power suite; b) clairsentients were described as precognitive, but had no power that could see the future; c) psions generally were cited as being particularly effective against Aberrants, but mechanically few of their powers gave them an edge over Aberrants greater than a neutral with sufficient tech. Various supplements addressed these discrepancies: the ISRA book gave clears precognition, the Players Guide freeform psi allowed for biokinetic healing, and somewhere in canon they suggested that psi and taint/quantum cancelled each other out, and that you could represent this by having psi and quantum powers concurrently fizzle giving psion strike teams a distinctive edge. It would be preferable to have this transparency up-front.<br /> <br /> (Addendum: the biokinetics were the ne plus ultra of infiltration in the fiction, but how did they get around the fact that every single psion (and some devices) could detect them by using Attunement? Not to mention the Clairsentient powers that could thwart them. I can imagine some ways they could do it, but I'd like the glaringly obvious disparity to be addressed).<br /> <br /> 3. Fewer rolls. Trinity was an advance in the Storyteller system by having Armor/Soak automatically deducted from damage, instead of rolled. (They also were advanced in having a static 'difficulty number' of 7. Ah binary distributions.) You still had to roll attack, dodge/parry, and damage as separate gobs of d10s. Also initiative rolls. We can simplify. We can use more static mods!<br /> <br /> 4. Change or eliminate Qualities. I hate reroll mechanics. They throw off my precious binary distributions!<br /> <br /> 5. Front and center clarity that every psi Order has members from (mostly!) every Aptitude. This was established fairly early on but the idea that each Order was monolithic stuck in the heads of many players. Diversity of options is attractive!<br /> <br /> 6. Having the South American psi group structured as a criminal family/ drug cartel made no sense and was a little offensive. As a biotech company crossed with a transhuman project? Much more interesting. NORCA was all these things, but I hope for an emphasis on the latter.<br /> <br /> 7. The UAN was presented as one of the most prominent geopolitical powers, if not THE most. Yet they were barely mentioned in the fiction. I guess being peaceful and affluent is boring and not conducive to fiction, but I'd love to see more African cultural influences on the setting as a whole. Maybe more Swahili slang in space.<br /> <br /> 8. Related to (7) above: the Chinese made first contact with the first alien species, so they got called the &quot;Qin.&quot; The Karroo miners, a subculture of the UAN, made first contact with the second alien species so they got named... the &quot;Chromatics&quot;? Why not use an African name? (I did in my game.)<br /> <br /> 9. The Coalition as rape aliens was poorly executed. The rape made no sense, the biology made no sense, and the subgroups looked like muppets (not sure that last one follows). Their being genestealers with advanced technology was great, and I loved the reveal that their socialization was pheremone based (just as Qin were telepathy-based and the Chromatics were light pattern-based; it contrasted with humans as linguistically-based). If you must have rape aliens, I prefer space wasp (xenomorphs!) or succubus models.<br /> <br /> 10. If you can, avoid or give context to headscratcher statements like &quot;Unless you want me to carve a pair of these into you, I'd turn the camera off,&quot; (Trinity, p.57) or &quot;your gender [male] can't have children.&quot; (Shattered Europe, p.133). Did I mention that I nitpick?<br /> <br /> 11. Give additional clarity to the technologies that are ubiquitous in the future. It took me quite a while to figure out that hover vehicles used ducted fans rather than some kind of anti-gravity. (Maybe that was just me being slow.) I am being a little unfair, fusion rockets and computer agents were fairly well-detailed in the main book and many other technologies were explained well in the tech manual. And I admire the tech manual for giving equal room to peaceful tech as they did to standard RPG adventurer murder-hobo weapon tech.<br /> <br /> 12. Eliminate or change Psionic Backlash. This is a holdover of White Wolf games where the better a character got at some supernatural stat, the worse off he was mechanically in some way. (Rage in Werewolf: the Apocalypse is a good parallel example). Psionic Backlash is used arbitrarily and punitively in the Darkness Revealed series of adventures; page 91 in Passage Through Shadow calls for &quot;All Players roll Psi to resist backlash&quot; due to the arrival of a Chromatic jumpship. This is contrary to the corebook rule that backlash events be &quot;within the range of your character's Attunement,&quot; which may be as little as five meters. It was, in effect, instructing the gamemaster to cheat to fuck over the PCs. (Not that I'm wholly innocent of that, but still, bad form). Also, Psionic Backlash raises the question how powerful Clears aren't taking Bashing damage constantly; I think somewhere it is mentioned this is one reason why Otha is such a recluse, but that sucks, and sucks especially for PCs.<br /> <br /> 13. Clarify psi prints (Trinity, p.194). Can any psion sense them? Is detecting them really a prerequisite to the usage of some powers? It is hardly mentioned anywhere else in the rules or the fiction, how does it all fit? (In my game, any psion could do it, but only Clears and Telepaths were told about it during training).<br /> <br /> Whew, I've been waiting 15 years to get some of these off my chest. Thanks for reading my rant!","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3453-nephandi","name":"Nephandi","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3453_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"22"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-07-10T00:28:43-07:00","id":193235,"title":"","content":"I do appreciate that many of my complaints will likely be moot in the reboot, which will have new mechanics. Hooray!<br /> <br /> But I would also like to echo a part of the original post. 14. Eliminate time delay for Tranlocation's Long Jump. Time delays were not an aspect of teleportation in the Darkness Revealed adventures when the PCs jump around with Mayor N'gamba. Nor with Clarence Greaves in Alien Encounter: Invasion. Other parts of the Stellar Frontiers book suggest that teleportation is instantaneous.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3453-nephandi","name":"Nephandi","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3453_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"22"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-09-15T22:22:47-07:00","id":257886,"title":"","content":"Wow - I don't know how I missed that Trinity was coming back, but I saw the poster release and followed up and now I am super excited that both my favorite old White Wolf games are getting a new coat of paint and are hitting the road again. I have been following the Mage posts excitedly and now I have something else to follow with baited breath as well.<br /> <br /> I will be honest though, and admit that I haven't cracked open a Trinity book in close to 10 years, so I pulled out my old spiral bound copy, checked to make sure no pages had fallen out, and started reading the colored setting section. I don't know how much of the setting revisions have already been completed and firmed up, but I did walk away with a list of things I can hope get a good looking over.<br /> <br /> Caveat to everything that follows - It has been a long time since I have read the various source books, so some of these may have been addressed in the original setting, others are simply my &quot;wish list&quot; opinions.<br /> <br /> 1) It sounds like instead of a strict Trinity Timeline we are getting the Trinity Continuum, which in the words of the Doctor, will have all sorts of timey-whimey oddness. If this lets the 20's era have lost worlds and hollow earths while explaining why they don't exist in the now or future I am completely cool with this. I am personally hoping that the various Telluric energy events brings them into and out of alignments with the various eras.<br /> <br /> 2) Please no references to 70's &quot;super-normal events' and &quot;unusual individuals.&quot; I am cool with the introduction of other eras, but I could never buy that people alive during both the 70's and the Aberrant era didn't put two and two together. Isolated Inspired throughout history is cool though.<br /> <br /> 3) Which leads me to Project Rewrite - I am cool with a huge amount of data being lost, but the entire idea that Aeon Trinity is the only organization controlling the rebuilding of a knowledge database for the world is nuts.<br /> <br /> 4) Aeon Trinity, while I love the place it has in the history of the setting, could it please be dialed back some. It is described as having &quot;hundreds of thousands of agents.&quot; the entire US government has 400K+ employees. The UN has about 50K staff and about 80K peacekeepers with a combined 2 year budget of around 12-13 billion for both. I'll admit that Aeon Trinity is described as doing a lot, but is it really a 200K+ organization? How is it financed? The US does it through taxation, the UN through member nations contributions. Where is Aeon Trinity raking in the money to finance everything?<br /> <br /> 5) Hopefully the setting reboot will deal with technology that has become ubiquitous over the last 16 odd years. Some tech I would really like to see address<br /> A) Drones - are they being used in the future, why use psions when you can drone strike an Abberant? I personally would love it if the future is drone phobic because too many Aberrant found ways to control them and use them against their operators. With commercial applications of drones being developed right now as well, if drones are still around are they really being used to deliver pizza and beer to college dormrooms everywhere in 2120?<br /> B) Social Media - I think I read already that wireless communication is back, so it sounds like the Comm Crunch is gone or modified. If that is the case, then I am down with that. Communication technologies, social media, surveillance concerns are all far more interesting to me as social pressures than nobody being able to figure out how to build secure decentralized communication systems with redundant back ups just to provide a tax source. Considering how social media dependent parts of society is now, it would be iteresting to see how the loss of the OpNet and then its return affect it. Also with various social media driven events like various Arab Spring protests, It would be interesting to see how social media affects the battlefield of 2120. A team of heroes could actually be formed when they all get an app alert of threat in their area and respond.<br /> C) 3-D Printing - Its already possible to make working plastic guns at home. Advance the technology and add in Hyperfusion power sources and we begin to verge on post consumer economies. Blue prints and raw resources could become key economic drivers.<br /> <br /> 6) As a Texan, I would ask that the Tex-Mex district be renamed if it exists in the Trinity Continuum. Tex-Mex is a style of food.<br /> <br /> 7) I know I already saw a comment that lay out style would be updated, but just my two cents - please no weird squashed face hologram images for the various personalities in the setting. I didn't like those graphics 16 years ago and they haven't gotten any better with time.<br /> <br /> 8) I doubt this would every happen, since its so key to the setting, but could we please not destroy the Louvre. If I had the cash I could easily spend a month in Paris and visit the Louvre every day. I've visited museums on 5 continents in it is one of my favorites. I know that Apocalyptic settings always like to destroy France/Paris. it's so cliche at this point that I just roll my eyes when I see it happen. I like the idea of a shattered Europe, I would just like the space station to hit a different region. My personal preference would be Rome. For some reason I really like the idea of a Catholic Church without a seat of power and the newly elected Pope being a Dali Lama sort of international pilgrim.<br /> <br /> 9) Religion, I know it can be a touchy subject, but if the setting continues to have religiously motivated Aberrants decimate huge portions of the globe, I would really like to know how 20th century religions shake out in 2120. About 16% of the worlds population is already non-religious, and that jumps up to as much as 25% in western industrial nations like the UK. Super powered beings, super powered religious terrorists, world war, psions, aliens all should have a profound effects. The setting gave some brief mentions to this issues 16 years ago, and hope we see the evolution of religions explored in the reboot.<br /> <br /> 10) If Scotland votes to split from the UK on Thursday, I hope that makes it into the new setting as well. Of course, since they will be depending on the North Sea oil fields to help pay for their new economy, it will suck for them when hyperfusion is developed and crashes oil based economies.<br /> <br /> Ok - that's enough for now. Time to randomly crack open one of the other source books and reread it.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":3385,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3385-ckobbe","user":"ckobbe","date":". 09-16-2014, 10:09 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3385-ckobbe","name":"ckobbe","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"151"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-09-15T23:05:41-07:00","id":257903,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>ckobbe</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/trinity/trinity-continuum-\u00e6on/148684-what-i-want-to-see-in-a-new-aeon-trinity-reboot?p=257886#post257886\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">1) It sounds like instead of a strict Trinity Timeline we are getting the Trinity Continuum, which in the words of the Doctor, will have all sorts of timey-whimey oddness. If this lets the 20's era have lost worlds and hollow earths while explaining why they don't exist in the now or future I am completely cool with this. I am personally hoping that the various Telluric energy events brings them into and out of alignments with the various eras.</div> </div> </div> </div>That won't be the principle we operate on, but it's as valid an explanation as any.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> 2) Please no references to 70's &quot;super-normal events' and &quot;unusual individuals.&quot; I am cool with the introduction of other eras, but I could never buy that people alive during both the 70's and the Aberrant era didn't put two and two together. Isolated Inspired throughout history is cool though. </div> </div> </div>Sorry. &quot;Every Age Has Its Heroes&quot; isn't just a snappy slogan.<br /> <br /> Just because they exist, however, that does not necessarily mean that the public is aware.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> 4) Aeon Trinity, while I love the place it has in the history of the setting, could it please be dialed back some. It is described as having &quot;hundreds of thousands of agents.&quot; the entire US government has 400K+ employees. The UN has about 50K staff and about 80K peacekeepers with a combined 2 year budget of around 12-13 billion for both. I'll admit that Aeon Trinity is described as doing a lot, but is it really a 200K+ organization? How is it financed? The US does it through taxation, the UN through member nations contributions. Where is Aeon Trinity raking in the money to finance everything? </div> </div> </div>Current projections show the world population continuing to grow until at least 2050 with as many as 11 billion people, and the Aeon timeline is 70 years further on from that. Aeon is an organization which covered all of settled space, including Luna. There are agents in extrasolar colonies.<br /> <br /> 200K+ might be a stretch in the present, but I don't think it's unreasonable for the 2120s.<br /> <br /> Mercer had a lot of seed money to get the Aeon Society started, and continued to grow that with a number of lucrative patents. I would imagine that, given Aeon's habit of recruiting the best and brightest, they've continued in this vein with new patented inventions. There are a lot of ways to make money. Given Mercer's reputation as a philanthropist, Aeon would probably capitalize on that with their own fundraising efforts.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> 8) I doubt this would every happen, since its so key to the setting, but could we please not destroy the Louvre. If I had the cash I could easily spend a month in Paris and visit the Louvre every day. I've visited museums on 5 continents in it is one of my favorites. </div> </div> </div>The real world is not so nice as to avoid tragedy in cultural centres. Otherwise we still wouldn't be pissed off about the destruction of the Library of Alexandria.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> I know that Apocalyptic settings always like to destroy France/Paris. it's so cliche at this point that I just roll my eyes when I see it happen. </div> </div> </div>I can't think of any others offhand, particularly not from media predating 1997.<br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b><span style=\"color:#800000\">Ian A. A. Watson</span></b><span style=\"color:#bdc3c7\">(he/she)</span><br /> <b>Onyx Path Community Manager<br /> Trinity Continuum Content Lead</b>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4-ianwatson","name":"IanWatson","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar4_2.png","title":"Community Manager","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1512"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-09-16T06:18:15-07:00","id":258068,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>IanWatson</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/trinity/trinity-continuum-\u00e6on/148684-what-i-want-to-see-in-a-new-aeon-trinity-reboot?p=257903#post257903\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I can't think of any others offhand, particularly not from media predating 1997.</div> </div> </div> </div> <b>Top 10 films that destroyed Paris</b><br /> <br /> <a href=\"http://www.independent.co.uk/arts-entertainment/films/features/top-10-films-that-destroyed-paris-2312467.html\" target=\"_blank\">http://www.independent.co.uk/arts-en...s-2312467.html</a><br /> <br /> <b><a href=\"http://io9.com/5943601/the-eiffel-tower-who-destroyed-it-best\" target=\"_blank\">The Eiffel Tower: Who destroyed it best?</a></b><br /> <br /> <a href=\"http://io9.com/5943601/the-eiffel-tower-who-destroyed-it-best\" target=\"_blank\">http://io9.com/5943601/the-eiffel-to...troyed-it-best</a><br /> <br /> There is also the Paris Must be Destroyed Android game app.<br /> <br /> To be fair, at least part of the reason Paris is destoyed so often has to be how visually iconic it is with Notre Dame/ the Louvre Glass Pyramid/Arc de Triomphe/Eiffel Tower. I would be willing to bet that when a city needs to be destroyed in western media, outside of US cities like New York, Paris has to contend with the top spot with London.<br /> <br /> I get what you are saying about destroyed cultural centers and tragedy - and I agree. But if I had my one personal dream preference for changing the setting, this would be it.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3385-ckobbe","name":"ckobbe","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"151"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-09-16T06:42:53-07:00","id":258079,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>IanWatson</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/trinity/trinity-continuum-\u00e6on/148684-what-i-want-to-see-in-a-new-aeon-trinity-reboot?p=257903#post257903\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Current projections show the world population continuing to grow until at least 2050 with as many as 11 billion people, and the Aeon timeline is 70 years further on from that. Aeon is an organization which covered all of settled space, including Luna. There are agents in extrasolar colonies.<br /> <br /> 200K+ might be a stretch in the present, but I don't think it's unreasonable for the 2120s.<br /> <br /> Mercer had a lot of seed money to get the Aeon Society started, and continued to grow that with a number of lucrative patents. I would imagine that, given Aeon's habit of recruiting the best and brightest, they've continued in this vein with new patented inventions. There are a lot of ways to make money. Given Mercer's reputation as a philanthropist, Aeon would probably capitalize on that with their own fundraising efforts.</div> </div> </div> </div>I can buy into part of that explanation, especially if it is called out as such, but it would still have to be a hell of a revenue stream if it brings in the double digit billions year after year for Aeon Trinity to even have a low level of funding.<br /> <br /> Aeon Trinity is already presented as being up in everyone's business. I could see them having a tighter focused core that accomplishes its goals through affilations with and directing other groups. Masters of Bureaucratic Aikido. A soup kitchen doesn't need to be run by Aeon Trinity, but if its affilated with them, it hooks into a greater charity network that coordinated resources and personnel. Other focus areas could be similar. You still get huge numbers of affiliates/resources, a presence across known space, but would explain a much lower revenue base.<br /> <br /> I also like the idea of a PC group being able to be more of a star in the organization, not agent group #3,217.<br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3385-ckobbe","name":"ckobbe","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"151"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-09-16T07:00:08-07:00","id":258085,"title":"","content":"Ian - thanks for the redirect - don't know why I didn't think to look for an already existing thread. I also enjoyed the reply <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/smile.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Smile\" smilieid=\"1\" class=\"inlineimg\" /><br /> <br /> I did have two other thoughts since last night.<br /> <br /> 1) With the incredible attention to diversity with gender/ethnicity/nationality/religion portrayed, it would also be nice for some LGBT representation.<br /> <br /> 2) Arcologies - I'm not sure if each time they are referred to if they mean giant self contained self-sufficient hyper structures, mega city sprawls, walled city enclaves, or other possible planned or evolved living spaces. Except for space and undersea habitats, they all seem to be mentioned as existing at preexisting cities. Are they new hyperstructures that could be built in the sq.km. devastation left after multiple city blocks were leveled (i.e Metropolis at the end of <i>Man of Steel</i>) or are they repurposed/updated structures that have survived a century of conflict (i.e. Chicago in <i>Divergence</i>). It would be nice to know which cities are which type. There is a huge difference between Masdar City <a href=\"http://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Masdar_City\" target=\"_blank\">http://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Masdar_City</a> and Crystal Island <a href=\"http://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Crystal_Island\" target=\"_blank\">http://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Crystal_Island</a>","signature":"","edited":{"userid":3385,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3385-ckobbe","user":"ckobbe","date":". 09-16-2014, 10:03 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3385-ckobbe","name":"ckobbe","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"151"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-09-16T08:05:21-07:00","id":258151,"title":"","content":"About the only thing I would want adjusted is a better end scenario for Divas Mal. I understand that the character is depicted with a setting-warping degree of power and is nearly unassailable in most respects, but something about a figure so important to 2 thirds of the story quietly sitting out the third act seems...anticlimactic.<br /> He doesn't necessarily have to come storming back on stage with great vengeance and furious anger, but doing something more interesting than vanishing into his own universe would be appreciated.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1420009-the-artificer-s-workshop\" target=\"_blank\">The Artificer's Workshop</a> - A collection of Exalted Artifacts<br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/806809-curios-relics-and-tomes\" target=\"_blank\">Curios, Relics, and Tomes</a> - A collection of Relics (Cursed and Otherwise)<br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/793173-the-horror-show\" target=\"_blank\">The Horror Lab</a> - A collection of Beasts, Monsters and less definable things.<br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/1128197-strange-places#post1128197\" target=\"_blank\">Strange Places</a> - A collection of Dark, Mysterious, and Wondrous Locations<br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/993181-twilight-menagerie\" target=\"_blank\">Twilight Menagerie</a> - A collection of Ephemeral Entities","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/775-reighnhell","name":"Reighnhell","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar775_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"749"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-09-16T08:21:09-07:00","id":258168,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>ckobbe</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/trinity/trinity-continuum-\u00e6on/148684-what-i-want-to-see-in-a-new-aeon-trinity-reboot?p=258068#post258068\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"> <b>Top 10 films that destroyed Paris</b><br /> <br /> <a href=\"http://www.independent.co.uk/arts-entertainment/films/features/top-10-films-that-destroyed-paris-2312467.html\" target=\"_blank\">http://www.independent.co.uk/arts-en...s-2312467.html</a><br /> <br /> <b><a href=\"http://io9.com/5943601/the-eiffel-tower-who-destroyed-it-best\" target=\"_blank\">The Eiffel Tower: Who destroyed it best?</a></b><br /> <br /> <a href=\"http://io9.com/5943601/the-eiffel-tower-who-destroyed-it-best\" target=\"_blank\">http://io9.com/5943601/the-eiffel-to...troyed-it-best</a><br /> <br /> There is also the Paris Must be Destroyed Android game app.<br /> <br /> To be fair, at least part of the reason Paris is destoyed so often has to be how visually iconic it is with Notre Dame/ the Louvre Glass Pyramid/Arc de Triomphe/Eiffel Tower. I would be willing to bet that when a city needs to be destroyed in western media, outside of US cities like New York, Paris has to contend with the top spot with London.<br /> <br /> I get what you are saying about destroyed cultural centers and tragedy - and I agree. But if I had my one personal dream preference for changing the setting, this would be it.</div> </div> </div> </div>There are very few large, international and iconic cities that have easily discernible skylines and universally recognized landmarks.<br /> <br /> When cities have to be destroyed, particularly in a montage, New York, Washington, Los Angeles, Paris, Hong Kong, Tokyo, London, etc. are the natural targets. They might as well paint bulls-eyes on the White House, Empire State Building, Statue of Liberty, Hollywood Sign, Sydney Opera House, Pyramids, Big Ben, and of course, the Eiffel Tower. Besides, Paris is also one of the few non-Anglo cities that has such immediate worldwide acclaim and recognition.<br /> <br /> Sorry, in any apocalyptic or alien invasion scenario, Paris has to go. I suggest they build a lot of bomb shelters. <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/smile.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Smile\" smilieid=\"1\" class=\"inlineimg\" />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":618,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/618-branford","user":"branford","date":". 09-16-2014, 01:29 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/618-branford","name":"branford","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar618_2.gif","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1904"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-09-16T08:56:30-07:00","id":258192,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>branford</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/trinity/trinity-continuum-\u00e6on/148684-what-i-want-to-see-in-a-new-aeon-trinity-reboot?p=258168#post258168\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Sorry, in any apocalyptic or alien invasion scenario, Paris has to go. I suggest they build a lot of bomb shelters. <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/smile.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Smile\" smilieid=\"1\" class=\"inlineimg\" /></div> </div> </div> </div>LOL - maybe bomb shelters is how Aeon Trinity made a lot of its cash <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/wink.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Wink\" smilieid=\"4\" class=\"inlineimg\" />.<br /> <br /> As an aside, I've visited and been in the pyramids, and they never get the surroundings right in the movies. I mean I got a shot glass from the Hard Rock Cafe across the street from the pyramids. They never show that urbanization has come right up to them or the literal tons of trash surrounding the area.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3385-ckobbe","name":"ckobbe","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"151"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-09-16T12:54:33-07:00","id":258384,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>ckobbe</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/trinity/trinity-continuum-\u00e6on/148684-what-i-want-to-see-in-a-new-aeon-trinity-reboot?p=258085#post258085\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">1) With the incredible attention to diversity with gender/ethnicity/nationality/religion portrayed, it would also be nice for some LGBT representation.</div> </div> </div> </div>Original Aberrant was one of the first RPGs to feature a transwoman (London Fog). We're proud of that. I can guarantee that will continue.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Reighnhell</strong> </div> <div class=\"message\">About the only thing I would want adjusted is a better end scenario for Divas Mal. I understand that the character is depicted with a setting-warping degree of power and is nearly unassailable in most respects, but something about a figure so important to 2 thirds of the story quietly sitting out the third act seems...anticlimactic.<br /> He doesn't necessarily have to come storming back on stage with great vengeance and furious anger, but doing something more interesting than vanishing into his own universe would be appreciated.</div> </div> </div> </div>As one of the founders of the Aeon Society, Donighal wasn't really any more or less important than anyone else, most of whom are dead (or MIA) after the Adventure! era.<br /> <br /> While he did found an additional organization -- the Teragen -- in the Aberrant era, he spends most of that era out of the picture in Chrysalis.<br /> <br /> His role has taken on a lot greater importance in the eyes of many fans since the original publication, but with few exceptions he's always been a background element. I don't really see the need for anything beyond the sort of story he already had.<br /> <br /> If you don't think killing the UN Secretary-General and disappearing to create his own universe is interesting, I really don't know how to answer that.<br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b><span style=\"color:#800000\">Ian A. A. Watson</span></b><span style=\"color:#bdc3c7\">(he/she)</span><br /> <b>Onyx Path Community Manager<br /> Trinity Continuum Content Lead</b>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":5}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4-ianwatson","name":"IanWatson","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar4_2.png","title":"Community Manager","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1512"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-09-16T22:11:09-07:00","id":258717,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Reighnhell</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/trinity/trinity-continuum-\u00e6on/148684-what-i-want-to-see-in-a-new-aeon-trinity-reboot?p=258151#post258151\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">About the only thing I would want adjusted is a better end scenario for Divas Mal. I understand that the character is depicted with a setting-warping degree of power and is nearly unassailable in most respects, but something about a figure so important to 2 thirds of the story quietly sitting out the third act seems...anticlimactic.<br /> He doesn't necessarily have to come storming back on stage with great vengeance and furious anger, but doing something more interesting than vanishing into his own universe would be appreciated.</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> I'd appreciate toning down his RELATIVE power (compared to Nova PCs) - specifically his writeup included broad-stroak abilities that were clearly there for no other reason than to protect the metaplot from PCs - a design philosophy that should generally be avoided.<br /> <br /> Also if you're going to put him at that power level and have the whole Chrysalis thing you need to actually address what his inhuman features are - and &quot;inhumanly perfect looking&quot; is only 1 feature.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Check out my expansion to the <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/185084-autochthonia-house-material\" target=\"_blank\">Realm of Brass and Shadow</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1098-glamourweaver","name":"glamourweaver","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1098_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"7541"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-09-17T06:23:34-07:00","id":258939,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>IanWatson</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/trinity/trinity-continuum-\u00e6on/148684-what-i-want-to-see-in-a-new-aeon-trinity-reboot?p=258384#post258384\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Original Aberrant was one of the first RPGs to feature a transwoman (London Fog). We're proud of that. I can guarantee that will continue.</div> </div> </div> </div>I was unaware of her - Aberrant was actually the game I was least invested in of the three, although I was kind of aware of Divas Mal's status. Interestingly while reading Poxy Zweidler's bio in Shattered Europe last night I saw that he had a toss away line that could code him as bisexual, which I was also not aware of.<br /> <br /> I think I saw somewhere that the vitakinetics are moving more towards a search and rescue/paramedic sort of role in new Trinity. I do hope that we don't completely lose the mad medical/scientist angle though. I know at its core Trinity isn't intended to be a horror game, but the medical realm has always lent itself so well to the genre. Whether is the personal horror when a body turns against itself (disease/cancer), malpractice, medical experimentation (Tuskegee experiments/Nazi experiments/LSD trials) to simple inhuman practices (forced sterilizations/conversion therapies), medicine has plenty of real life horror - add in the fantastical of the Trinity Continuum and it's fertile ground for story-telling. When I GMed Darkness Revealed back in the day it was a fun but dark campaign, we really embraced the horror elements.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3385-ckobbe","name":"ckobbe","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"151"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-09-21T13:12:26-07:00","id":262418,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>ckobbe</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/trinity/trinity-continuum-\u00e6on/148684-what-i-want-to-see-in-a-new-aeon-trinity-reboot?p=257886#post257886\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">C) 3-D Printing - Its already possible to make working plastic guns at home. Advance the technology and add in Hyperfusion power sources and we begin to verge on post consumer economies. Blue prints and raw resources could become key economic drivers.</div> </div> </div> </div>Serendipitous considering I brought this up last week, but I just found this article.<br /> <br /> <b>3D printer heading to space could enable lunar exploration</b><br /> <br /> <a href=\"http://www.cnet.com/news/3d-printer-heading-to-space-could-enable-lunar-exploration/\" target=\"_blank\">http://www.cnet.com/news/3d-printer-...r-exploration/</a><br /> <br /> A couple of things that they are also working on that really jumped out at me were also the recycler for 3d printed material and especially the printer that would use regolith as feed material.<br /> <br /> For some other interesting possibilities...<br /> <br /> <b>5 startups that could radically transform the world around us</b><br /> <br /> <a href=\"http://techcitynews.com/2014/09/19/5-startups-that-could-radically-transform-the-world-around-us/\" target=\"_blank\">http://techcitynews.com/2014/09/19/5...rld-around-us/</a><br /> <br /> It would be interesting if everyone in 2120 drank water from Ooho! globs, especially since Trinity already has such a biotech slant.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":3385,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3385-ckobbe","user":"ckobbe","date":". 09-21-2014, 04:20 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3385-ckobbe","name":"ckobbe","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"151"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-09-27T22:45:26-07:00","id":267225,"title":"","content":"Mostly I just want psions to get a small power boost, the system to scale a little better, the systems to integrate a little better, some stuff that originally didn't get as much coverage getting more coverage, and maybe a few Aberrant powers tweaked. Since that seems to be the goal of the design, I'm pretty sure I'll be happy with whatever they choose to do.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1136-wolfgar","name":"Wolfgar","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1136_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"646"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-10-03T07:49:05-07:00","id":271619,"title":"","content":"Well my almost only problem with Aberrant is how expensive the powers are to use. Especially the multiple technique having .level 3 powers coating from 3-6 Quantum a pop. With pools of around 20-30 Quantum you really can't fire them of that often and trying to practice such powers usage will mean your pool is empty within 10 minutes of intense practice which encompasses perhaps 5-10 uses of said powers. That is unless you, possess Node 3+ and, practice near the Sun or a Nuclear reactor where you can regenerate Quantum at considerable rate.<br /> <br /> Let alone basic movement powers like flight, hypermovement etc. cost 2+ Quantum and these kind of powers should be pretty basic. When have you ever seen a superpowers genre where the protagonist, or antagonist for that matter, wore himself down from excessive use of flight power?<br /> <br /> Aside from that the other problem (?) is with Taint, and by extension Chrysalis, and the rate of it's gain. I have a Quantum 5 character, started at Q3 I think, that I have played for several years and he has not gained a single temporary Taint throughout the game, his Permanent taint of 2 is the result of having Q5 and Node 3, and only 1 point of temporary Chrysalis, and that only because after being thought how to channel Chrysalis he has actively tried to risk things a lot to gain points in it. All in all it seems literally impossible to ever have enough Chrysalis to actually try to activate it.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1629-possessed","name":"Possessed","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1629_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1140"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-10-03T13:50:22-07:00","id":271723,"title":"","content":"Not enough juice to fly? Sounds like you need nimbus from DBZ! (Ugghhh joking really I swear!) We use the variants from the players guide on how to keep from running out of power too quick, because true-a pool of 24-26 aint gonnna cut it if you are a q bolt characterin a fight with a dozen bad guys...well it would cut it if you only hit each of them once and had no other powers that cost quantum. So really, id just like those pg variants in the core.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><img class=\"bbcode-attachment js-need-data-att-update\" src=\"filedata/fetch?filedataid=392\" data-tempid=\"temp_392_1519878565794_106\" />","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3676-manbearpig","name":"ManBearPig","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3676_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Aug 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"148"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-10-03T22:39:11-07:00","id":272046,"title":"","content":"Yeah there are variants in the PG true but I do think these things should be in taken into account with the new core (as I now noticed you saying as well), though even something as simple as the stunt system of Exalted/Scion would help the matter considerably, along with other adjustments to the system.<br /> <br /> When I ST Aberrant, which is to say somewhat rarely as usually if we play it we continue on the long game where I am a player, I tend to gloss over most of the costs for powers. For example I allow people to use hypermovement and flight with no cost etc. and in some games I haven't even calculated their Q pools at all so they have more cinematic access to their power sets more limited by consequences of their actions than a pool of expendable juice. Yes this tends to lead to more high-powered games but then again I do think that is kinda the point in the genre.<br /> <br /> Still I know that such a style of gaming is not for everyone and would prefer if the rules were such that I wouldn't need to use alternatives and preferably neither would others. So a power pool in itself isn't bad way to restrict player mojo but it should not be so strict as to leave the powers to the sidelines especially in a game like Aberrant where the point is in the slow growth of the characters from humans into Novas and very slowly from there to inhuman Godhood, and the consequences and choices done along that road.<br /> <br /> As a fun little side note, non of our group has Q-Bolt and only one has the Elemental Controls equivalent Technique. Which tends to mean no cheap ways to deal damage and such which leads to use of more powerful, generally not in combat, abilities creatively and tends to burn through the Q-pool rather quickly.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1629-possessed","name":"Possessed","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1629_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1140"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-10-04T01:05:08-07:00","id":272102,"title":"","content":"We just started a low power game. My quantum is 1. My powers are absorbtion and armor at 1. No stat above 3. Its a pretty mean street almost &quot;alphas&quot; like game, since no one really spends quantum for the most part (except when I get shot). Lots of fun...but im pretty sure a starting dynamic could give me a run for my money off the bat.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><img class=\"bbcode-attachment js-need-data-att-update\" src=\"filedata/fetch?filedataid=392\" data-tempid=\"temp_392_1519878565794_106\" />","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3676-manbearpig","name":"ManBearPig","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3676_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Aug 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"148"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-10-05T19:06:12-07:00","id":273406,"title":"","content":"Something more concrete:<br /> <br /> Cheaper powers. I would prefer some powers that I can use more often, or at will. 0 cost stuff is good. I don't need to be able to knock down buildings without effort, but my pyrokinetic should be able to light a cigarette for free (if such things even exist in his time), and my flying nova should really only have to spend energy on it if she needs to catch a jet mind-flight or something similar.<br /> <br /> Larger power pools. I like doing cool stuff. I don't really want to run out of my &quot;Do Cool Stuff&quot; juice mid-fight most scenes. It's fine once in a while for drama, but I would prefer it triggered by something specific, like a weakness or an energy draining counter-ability.<br /> <br /> Consistent stats across games. Seeing how there is going to be a universal core book, this shouldn't be hard.<br /> <br /> Biokinesis and Vitakinesis are going to need some readily identifiable thing that seperates them. I'm worried about the two getting goopy if biokinetics regenerate and vitakinetics can boost themselves.<br /> <br /> Psychokinetics need to be more powerful, and have less redundant powers. Since that's stated as a goal, groovy.<br /> <br /> Telepathy needs to be easier. Again, stated goal, yadda yadda.<br /> <br /> Mega-Attributes are gone, so their is no need to go into that.<br /> <br /> In general, nova powers need to be re-balanced to be a little closer. Offense should stay better than defense, because you get overly long combats otherwise, but maybe the gap shouldn't be as wide. Likewise if offense scales with Quantum (it probably won't) then so should defense.<br /> <br /> Adventure just needs more stuff. More stuff is good. I'd also like to see the invention system cross multiple eras.<br /> <br /> Setting wise, I'd like to see fewer named characters. The proxies, really famous people like world leaders, Aeon founders and a few of the more prominent novas are fine, but remembering all these people gets difficult. It's especially bad with Aberrant, as they tend to run over player creative space until it gets hard to not be a clone of someone else. I'd rather see more Duke Rollo style characters oddly; they give the setting a sense of realness without forcing out the PCs.<br /> <br /> I'd like to see Africa get some love.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1136-wolfgar","name":"Wolfgar","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1136_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"646"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-10-20T03:22:02-07:00","id":287386,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Wolfgar</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/trinity/trinity-continuum-\u00e6on/148684-what-i-want-to-see-in-a-new-aeon-trinity-reboot?p=273406#post273406\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Cheaper powers. I would prefer some powers that I can use more often, or at will. 0 cost stuff is good. I don't need to be able to knock down buildings without effort, but my pyrokinetic should be able to light a cigarette for free (if such things even exist in his time),</div> </div> </div> </div>This will absolutely be the case with Aeon - most 1 dot power use will cost 0 psi points.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> Biokinesis and Vitakinesis are going to need some readily identifiable thing that seperates them. I'm worried about the two getting goopy if biokinetics regenerate and vitakinetics can boost themselves. </div> </div> </div>Definitely. Part of the distinction is simple - biokinetics can give themselves inhuman abilities - wings, IR vision, gecko feet for sticking to walls, the ability to slither under a door... Vitakinetics can only enhance their existing abilities - if Wolverine (minus the claws and adamantium) or Captain America (movie version) can do something, so can they, and they can also enhance themselves in other ways. Also, Biokinetics can only heal or alter themselves, Vitakinetics can also heal and enhance others.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> I'd like to see Africa get some love. </div> </div> </div>I completely agree. It's getting a longer write-up in the core book, and will also be somewhat more important since (as I've mentioned previously) teleporters and Upeo members are options in the core book.<br /> <br /> <br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":96,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/96-john-snead","user":"John Snead","date":". 10-20-2014, 06:24 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/96-john-snead","name":"John Snead","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar96_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"34"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-10-21T12:03:12-07:00","id":288733,"title":"","content":"Excellent to hear. <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/smile.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Smile\" smilieid=\"1\" class=\"inlineimg\" />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1136-wolfgar","name":"Wolfgar","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1136_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"646"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-10-21T15:01:24-07:00","id":288982,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>John Snead</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/trinity/trinity-continuum-\u00e6on/148684-what-i-want-to-see-in-a-new-aeon-trinity-reboot?p=287386#post287386\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I completely agree. It's getting a longer write-up in the core book, and will also be somewhat more important since (as I've mentioned previously) teleporters and Upeo members are options in the core book.</div> </div> </div> </div>Great to hear about the extra attention being paid to Africa <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/smile.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Smile\" smilieid=\"1\" class=\"inlineimg\" /><br /> <br /> I'm curious to see how the mechanics shake out for Teleporters, as that kind of power set can unbalance a game with certain interpretations and I'm instinctively hesitant to allow it in-game. I liked the idea of the Order itself, and the porters powers in principle (manipulate space <i>somewhat</i>), but not the previous execution of some of those powers. I thought they could be <i>too</i> powerful individually (Long Jump, looking at you). I'm not suggesting that the other powers needing increasing in relative power, but '<i>any distance</i>' teleportation as a power for individual PCs was excessive, even with familiarity rules. I'd prefer stuff generally along the lines of Jump, Shimmer, Fading, Relay Person and so on.<br /> <br /> Should be an interesting read come open dev time.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"color:#ff0000\"><b>Ad Astra</b></span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/232-chill","name":"CHILL","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar232_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"248"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-10-23T12:55:06-07:00","id":290731,"title":"","content":"I'm not seeing an immediate issue with Long Jump. Care to explain?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1136-wolfgar","name":"Wolfgar","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1136_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"646"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-10-23T17:08:47-07:00","id":290859,"title":"","content":"Don't have the book to hand, but IIRC it allowed 'any distance' travel by a single porter. I'm not a fan of that level of power for an individual.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"color:#ff0000\"><b>Ad Astra</b></span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/232-chill","name":"CHILL","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar232_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"248"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-10-24T04:39:32-07:00","id":291190,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Scutarii</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/trinity/trinity-continuum-\u00e6on/148684-what-i-want-to-see-in-a-new-aeon-trinity-reboot?p=150292#post150292\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">As someone with no connection whatsoever to the game and only paid it attention after the mention it wil use similar mechanics to Scion I went and had a skim of the old Aeon book.<br /> <br /> A thing I noticed was that I'd basically never want to play as most of the archetypes. Not to say I wouldn't want someone with their powers...just not someone who <i>only</i> had those powers. Mostly it comes down to having some kind of cool visual flashy power to go along with something more cerebral. A Clarisentient for example is really cool...until I realised all I'd be doing in my minds eye is grimacing a lot.<br /> <br /> So I'd like to see something that makes it easy to get something flashier either in each of the archetypes or have the entry level powers of each of the different archetypes be flashier or more powerful. See how Blood and Smoke makes rank 1 in a Discipline a boiled down essentials version of each theme. So someone who is a full on Clarisentient could also grab something on the side for Biokinesis or the like that bonus power doesn't feel like something really boring like moderately altering the temperature.</div> </div> </div> </div>Well, the guy from Dead Zone could not serve at least a little as reference for a Clarisentient in game? Just a thought.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1147-baaldam","name":"Baaldam","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1147_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4937"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-10-24T13:32:18-07:00","id":291539,"title":"","content":"Honestly I don't think Long Jump is all that problematic as structured. It does mean a character can get out of dangerous situations quickly, but they can do that with Jump just as easily. Mostly the power seems useful for rapid retreat/escape. I mean, looking it over...<br /> <br /> <b>The party needs to get through a locked door or hidden area.</b> You can't teleport in, so Long Jump is useless here.<br /> <br /> <b>You need information out of an NPC.</b> Well, you can teleport away, but that's not solving anything. You can't teleport to his place to go through his stuff or things he loves to threaten them either, unless you are already familiar with them, in which case it's probably smarter to just to use your existing familiarity as leverage instead.<br /> <br /> <b>The party is trapped in a room and about to be gassed.</b> Well, you can escape, but that doesn't help everyone else, and you might not be able to get back. Really, being able to travel to the other side of the door would be way more helpful here.<br /> <br /> <b>You want to cross a chasm, get over a cliff, or cross a gate.</b> Jump already does these better.<br /> <br /> <b>You need to break in somewhere to rescue a hostage, steal data, or sabotage someone. </b>You likely can't teleport in unless it's a familiar location, and the ST should have some say in that. It will be easier to<i> get out</i>, but still pretty hard to <i>get in</i>.<br /> <br /> <b>You are in a vehicle chase.</b> Sure, you can escape quickly. You might be of more use to the rest of the group using a different power though, if you have them available.<br /> <br /> <b>You are attacked by an Aberrant.</b> Once again, you can get out quickly, but your friends are kind of boned, and now down a man.<br /> <br /> <b>You are captured.</b> You can easily retreat somewhere, but that doesn't mean they won't know where to find you again, and their are options for psi-dampening tech.<br /> <br /> I'm sure if it just rubs you the wrong way their isn't anything I can say that will make you like it, but I'm not seeing anything that just wows me with it's overall effectiveness.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1136-wolfgar","name":"Wolfgar","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1136_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"646"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-10-24T14:55:38-07:00","id":291589,"title":"","content":"Hey Wolfgar. <br /> <br /> Oh, I know about its flexibility. Its purely that there's no distance limits on it that I dislike.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"color:#ff0000\"><b>Ad Astra</b></span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/232-chill","name":"CHILL","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar232_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"248"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-10-27T00:05:33-07:00","id":293536,"title":"","content":"So what is it about the distance limits is off-putting?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1136-wolfgar","name":"Wolfgar","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1136_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"646"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-10-27T16:32:13-07:00","id":294266,"title":"","content":"Its two items, really. <br /> <br /> Breaking it down...<br /> <br /> First, its just a little more world-spanning power than I like for Psions. I prefer low powered characters in games I run, limiting heavy reliance just on powers and trying to avoid the world-spanning stuff (of which any distance porting is one example). <br /> <br /> This is just a personal preference, and something I'm aware that I'm highly unlikely to change. I'm the guy that twitches at level 4 and 5 Psi powers generally, though, so... <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/wink.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Wink\" smilieid=\"4\" class=\"inlineimg\" /><br /> <br /> It's nothing to do with the mechanics as written by the way, just not something I want to see in most of my games. <br /> <br /> For perspective, I actively avoid games like Aberrant (way too many mad powerz). I like games with 'low level' (horrible term), incidental powers generally speaking.<br /> <br /> Secondly, but less of a concern, is 'go anywhere' powers making for some troublesome games. It can lead to dividing the party more frequently and for longer potentially. It can lead to more work that I usually want to tackle, especially when I use un-modified or only slightly modified published scenarios. I rarely have the time these days to create my own. Add to this that my games are online in recent years, which has different nuances for keeping players focused. Sure, there are ways to work around all that but its easier to avoid some powers from the get go. For instance, I don't think I ran a Trin game where the porters were 'back' as PC's. So yeah, I'm actively hesitant about the rebooted timeline being 6 months after they are supposed to be back. I may end up writing them out - I liked them when they were part of history <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/biggrin.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Big Grin\" smilieid=\"3\" class=\"inlineimg\" /><br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"color:#ff0000\"><b>Ad Astra</b></span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/232-chill","name":"CHILL","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar232_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"248"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-11-02T12:09:12-08:00","id":300256,"title":"","content":"If no one else has said it. Trinity Era Novas and rules for having a Node-Brain. Also, I'd like a big book of alternate Sci Fi settings. Pulp explorations of a Lowellian Mars ala Bradbury and Burroughs. Settling distant worlds with Novas. A busy active Cyperpunk-ish solar system with Psions. And all kinds of other goodness.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/857-astromancer","name":"Astromancer","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar857_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2195"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-11-02T21:01:01-08:00","id":300724,"title":"","content":"Yes the &quot;low level&quot; or &quot;low power&quot; game/setting needs to have some marketing spin for it, I believe. Personally I'm so used to running gods and monsters in my games that it's hard to go back to cops and hobbits, but that is certainly a good play-style, and deserves a more complimentary label.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1136-wolfgar","name":"Wolfgar","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1136_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"646"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-11-03T12:01:40-08:00","id":301403,"title":"","content":"I just want all the ships. More small fighter/ shuttle to Millenium falcon sized, more frigate types (more nation variation or alien types) and more star trek sized capitol ships or dreadnaught style. Pappa needs his sci-fi to be onboard the &quot;most important npc&quot;","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><img class=\"bbcode-attachment js-need-data-att-update\" src=\"filedata/fetch?filedataid=392\" data-tempid=\"temp_392_1519878565794_106\" />","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3676-manbearpig","name":"ManBearPig","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3676_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Aug 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"148"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-11-03T13:22:41-08:00","id":301468,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Wolfgar</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/trinity/trinity-continuum-\u00e6on/148684-what-i-want-to-see-in-a-new-aeon-trinity-reboot?p=300724#post300724\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Yes the &quot;low level&quot; or &quot;low power&quot; game/setting needs to have some marketing spin for it, I believe. Personally I'm so used to running gods and monsters in my games that it's hard to go back to cops and hobbits, but that is certainly a good play-style, and deserves a more complimentary label.</div> </div> </div> </div>Yeah, it does need a bit of spin, heh.<br /> <br /> 'Low powered' / 'low level' seems to imply inferior or boring to some - whereas for me it means more interesting &amp; rewarding, but then that's a gaming problem generally I think. I see too many players looking too much for &amp; relying on 'kewl powerz' over personality, background, and so on. As a GM it can like playing a game of whackamole putting a stop to that style of play if it isn't your thing. <br /> <br /> I think one of the major achievements likely to come out of this reboot is that GM's should be able to run one game setting <i>without</i> the others / varied power types bleeding in if they want to. That lets me keep my Aeon free of Novas, and Astromancer can easily do the exact opposite. I'm eagerly looking forward to seeing how that has been pulled off as its a tall order, its something I know I certainly wouldn't be able to figure out with any workable scale, let alone elegance. Roll on open dev.<br /> <br /> Also, better ship system for Aeon. Yeah - I'm right there with ManBearPig on that one. <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/biggrin.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Big Grin\" smilieid=\"3\" class=\"inlineimg\" />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"color:#ff0000\"><b>Ad Astra</b></span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/232-chill","name":"CHILL","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar232_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"248"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-11-03T18:00:46-08:00","id":301630,"title":"","content":"Iconic characters. I think they have a different name for them but the idea is the same.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/886-nofather","name":"nofather","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar886_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11016"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-11-03T18:48:37-08:00","id":301672,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Astromancer</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/trinity/trinity-continuum-\u00e6on/148684-what-i-want-to-see-in-a-new-aeon-trinity-reboot?p=300256#post300256\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">If no one else has said it. Trinity Era Novas and rules for having a Node-Brain.</div> </div> </div> </div>It's part of the core Continuum design philosophy that all of the games be interlinked, and one of the benefits of running on the same base system.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> Iconic characters. I think they have a different name for them but the idea is the same. </div> </div> </div>Sigs! Signature characters are a big part of the Continuum.<br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b><span style=\"color:#B22222\">Neall Raemonn Price</span><br /> Beleaguered Scion Developer</b>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/137-neall","name":"Neall","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar137_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1204"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-11-03T20:49:44-08:00","id":301758,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>CHILL</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/trinity/trinity-continuum-\u00e6on/148684-what-i-want-to-see-in-a-new-aeon-trinity-reboot?p=301468#post301468\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">'Low powered' / 'low level' seems to imply inferior or boring to some - whereas for me it means more interesting &amp; rewarding, but then that's a gaming problem generally I think. I see too many players looking too much for &amp; relying on 'kewl powerz' over personality, background, and so on. As a GM it can like playing a game of whackamole putting a stop to that style of play if it isn't your thing.</div> </div> </div> </div>Two notes.<br /> <br /> One, I have seen weakness used for a substitute for character personality as well, it's it's not any more inherently interesting than over power. Power level is essentially divorced from personality in my mind, and a good character is good regardless of where they lie in the universe.<br /> <br /> Two, if that style of play isn't your thing, it's very important to communicate that with your players directly, and then you either need to compromise or find new people. This is a creative exercise; we shouldn't be shutting people down needlessly.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> I think one of the major achievements likely to come out of this reboot is that GM's should be able to run one game setting <i>without</i> the others / varied power types bleeding in if they want to. That lets me keep my Aeon free of Novas, and Astromancer can easily do the exact opposite. I'm eagerly looking forward to seeing how that has been pulled off as its a tall order, its something I know I certainly wouldn't be able to figure out with any workable scale, let alone elegance. Roll on open dev. </div> </div> </div>At the same time I would like a setting where the character types can easily be blended, because otherwise what is the bloody point of a shared setting? I'll tell you, the last thing I want from White Wolf is for them to hint at cross-compatability, then shit it up and treat me like the asshole for wanting it.&quot;Oh, well it will totally DESTROY the themes of the game, plus the mechanics are designed to prevent such a thing, but I suppose if you HAVE to for your overpowered munchkin goober-fest we can't really stop you and your money spends just as golden as anyone else.&quot; Don't do me any favors, guys.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1136-wolfgar","name":"Wolfgar","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1136_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"646"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-11-04T08:50:14-08:00","id":302236,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Wolfgar</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/trinity/trinity-continuum-\u00e6on/148684-what-i-want-to-see-in-a-new-aeon-trinity-reboot?p=301758#post301758\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">One, I have seen weakness used for a substitute for character personality as well, it's it's not any more inherently interesting than over power. Power level is essentially divorced from personality in my mind, and a good character is good regardless of where they lie in the universe.</div> </div> </div> </div>I agree completely, but in a couple decades GMing I've seen it occur disproportionately the other way around. Power can get in the way, especially with less experienced players.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Wolfgar</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/trinity/trinity-continuum-\u00e6on/148684-what-i-want-to-see-in-a-new-aeon-trinity-reboot?p=301758#post301758\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Two, if that style of play isn't your thing, it's very important to communicate that with your players directly, and then you either need to compromise or find new people.</div> </div> </div> </div>Oh sure - I would've thought that all went without saying . The thread is about what we want to see, and what I want to see is going to be different from others. I came to Aeon first. I don't want a ramp up in powers for Psions by too much and absolutely want Aeon material that can stand alone - even if there's interlinking as Neall reiterated above. I readily acknowledge this is selfish, but I'd like this without having to work too hard to untangle things in the printed material - again, less time spent re-writing stuff is an important consideration for me. I don't want much, I know <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/tongue.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Stick Out Tongue\" smilieid=\"5\" class=\"inlineimg\" /><br /> <br /> With this being a 'continuum' now, I'm aware I'm probably going to have to surgically remove the stuff I'm not interested in, more than I did for later books in 1st Ed Aeon.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Wolfgar</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/trinity/trinity-continuum-\u00e6on/148684-what-i-want-to-see-in-a-new-aeon-trinity-reboot?p=301758#post301758\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">This is a creative exercise; we shouldn't be shutting people down needlessly.</div> </div> </div> </div>I'm really sure what you're getting at there. Some power sets are too much for my game styles, so I write them out or ignore them when GMing (obviously that's communicated well in advance to players). That doesn't affect a player's ability to be creative and it doesn't 'shut them down'. Its communicating what I'm prepared to allow when I'm running Aeon.<br /> <br /> Of course, this is all moot until we get to open dev and start seeing how this is all being planned. There's been enough noise about better low through high power scaling, common base system but 'modular' continuum that I increasingly get the sense we'll all get what we're after. That's going to be quite an achievement if they pull it off.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Wolfgar</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/trinity/trinity-continuum-\u00e6on/148684-what-i-want-to-see-in-a-new-aeon-trinity-reboot?p=301758#post301758\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">At the same time I would like a setting where the character types can easily be blended, because otherwise what is the bloody point of a shared setting? I'll tell you, the last thing I want from White Wolf is for them to hint at cross-compatability, then shit it up and treat me like the asshole for wanting it.&quot;Oh, well it will totally DESTROY the themes of the game, plus the mechanics are designed to prevent such a thing, but I suppose if you HAVE to for your overpowered munchkin goober-fest we can't really stop you and your money spends just as golden as anyone else.&quot; Don't do me any favors, guys.</div> </div> </div> </div>Heh, no, that's fair enough. I guess its a matter of perspective. Aeon never was a shared setting for me so the question for me the direct opposite - 'why the hell would you, gah!'<br /> <br /> I came to Aeon first, and wasn't interested in the other settings that came along later - it worked well enough on its own for me. I'd like the option to easily keep Ab and A! as distant history. I'm really looking forward to seeing if the new system allows me to do that out of the box, so to speak. If we can have the options to use, or not, the rest of the continuum as we see fit then OPP may be onto something really interesting here.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"color:#ff0000\"><b>Ad Astra</b></span>","edited":{"userid":232,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/232-chill","user":"CHILL","date":". 11-04-2014, 11:57 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/232-chill","name":"CHILL","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar232_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"248"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-11-05T17:00:31-08:00","id":303871,"title":"","content":"The comic industry calls people with &quot;low level&quot; powers relative to the mainline supers &quot;street level&quot;, it sounds a bit better and it may be a good term to use here for those whose power level is toned down compared to the rest of their particular era.<br /> <br /> I started with Aberrant and then Aeon soon after. I started running them in parallel (after the Aberrant campaign got past the starting wobbles) with each influencing the other in a kind of causal loop and unified rules would have helped with that considerably. The campaign was still mostly Aberrant oriented with the Aeon having several false starts until I got India Underground and using that the Aeon part finally clicked.<br /> <br /> Having rules for the Upeo and Chibs and their modes, even sketchy ones, in the main book would have also helped considerably but I already said that in in more detail in an earlier post and so I will not go into it more now. Mostly the rules need a good cleaning and balance fix in general and some kind of good literary lead-in, especially Aberrant which suffers a bit from its contemporary sci-fi with superhero comic genre powers and some of the themes yet none of the usual trappings format which gives it a kind of &quot;tuxedo opera&quot;* feel that can make it hard to get traction with otherwise. It has some of the threading problems that Aeon has too but nowhere near as much.<br /> <br /> With Aeon/Trinity the problem is more one of finding a good place to start. All the elements are there in a kind of umbrella overview sense but from the point of view of the main book the ends of the plot threads are all tucked away like a ball of snippits yarn. Most settings material was either justifications for the game mechanics themselves, isolated and often contradictory random facts about the settings with little to get a clear picture of how it fits together, or else tightly focused lead-ins to modules that would come out later with little or nothing to do until then. A lot of it concerned the Upeo and Chibs and would have been natural places to start but the plot trail on those was deliberately cold and ultimately lead nowhere with nothing in the main book to support campaigns looking into them. The same with the aliens: vague descriptions and some foreshadowing but with no support and the way extrasolar space was glossed over it amounted to a clear &quot;you cannot go there yet&quot; message. I think the Devs got so focused on making a neat multi-modular puzzle that they lost touch with how it would look to someone just starting to run a game of Aeon without intimate knowledge of the whole thing.<br /> <br /> Both of the games (I am not directly familiar with Adventure! so I am leaving it out of this) need hooks that lead to somewhere other than an exit into supplementary books. The little vignettes about signature characters and whatnot are nice, but a bit more in the way of illustrating the environment of the game to give the ST something to work with would go further (though the signature character stuff could be made less self-contained and serve the same purpose. <br /> <br /> * For those who do not know what a tuxedo opera is, it is a play that is done without costumes and often very little in the way of set dressing and props. It had the odd look as if people from the audience simply went up on stage and started acting (and in fact it has even been done with the cast spread out in the audience and literally doing just that). It drags reality into the setting and weakens suspension of disbelief kind of like what happens in a lot of supposedly real investigatory &quot;reality shows&quot; but if done well the juxtaposition can lead to a decent &quot;do something different&quot; kind of show.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/869-bc001","name":"BC001","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar869_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"96"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-02-18T11:35:35-08:00","id":410378,"title":"","content":"Not sure if anyone has brought this up yet, but I noticed this recently. How is the set of powers listed in electromanipulation not simply another application of biokinesis or vitakinesis? At best you are messing with biological materials. A better expression of controlling electric current would be literally working with that force without needing the medium of biology to work through. You can control movement, heat, and cold via Psychokinesis, yet an Electrokinetic only has access to 1/3 of the actual utility of Electromagnetism even though the aptitude claims control over that very force. Why then can't electrokinetics simply move existing electricity discounting medium, and where is the magnetism aspect?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/765-darksol-aeternium","name":"Darksol-aeternium","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar765_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"392"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-02-18T12:26:33-08:00","id":410435,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Darksol-aeternium</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/trinity/trinity-continuum-\u00e6on/148684-what-i-want-to-see-in-a-new-aeon-trinity-reboot?p=410378#post410378\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">snipping 'whats with the fuzzy logic on powers separation</div> </div> </div> </div>From a setting perspective there's very specific reason why this is the case (cough *Doyen / Tanks* cough). It comes up in snippets in the setting material that the separation between the aptitudes and aptitude modes is strange / restrictive / makey no sensey.<br /> <br /> From a mechanics perspective? No idea. Down to the writer's preferences at the time I'd guess.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"color:#ff0000\"><b>Ad Astra</b></span>","edited":{"userid":232,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/232-chill","user":"CHILL","date":". 02-22-2015, 05:36 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/232-chill","name":"CHILL","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar232_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"248"}]},"thankedby":[]}]}